VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# Error tracking — Sentry, EU region (#644). All three are optional and all
# three are unset locally on purpose: leaving VITE_SENTRY_DSN empty disables
# reporting entirely, so development noise never reaches the production project.
#
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN goes to VERCEL (it is public — it ships in the bundle).
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://<key>@<org>.ingest.de.sentry.io/<project>
#
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN goes to VERCEL as well, and is secret. It is what uploads
# source maps, and the production frontend builds on Vercel — so a token that
# exists only here means production stack traces stay minified. Set it locally
# too if you want to verify an upload before pushing; `npm run build` then
# uploads and deletes the maps, and skips both when it is unset.
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=sntrys_...
#
# SENTRY_DSN (no VITE_ prefix) goes to SUPABASE SECRETS, for the edge functions:
#   supabase secrets set SENTRY_DSN=...
# Same DSN value; the separate name keeps it out of the browser bundle.
# SENTRY_DSN=https://<key>@<org>.ingest.de.sentry.io/<project>

# Asset CDN origin (#577). Leave unset to serve every bucket straight from
# Supabase Storage — that is the safe default and the current production state.
# When set, CDN-enabled buckets (see `cdn` in src/lib/storage/buckets.ts) resolve
# to `<this>/<bucket>/<path>`. Set the same value as the ASSET_CDN_URL Supabase
# secret, or Edge Functions will reject the URLs their own SSRF guard sees.
# VITE_ASSET_CDN_URL=https://cdn.dungeongrimoire.com

# Cloudflare R2 (#577 stage 2) — where the bytes for R2-backed buckets live.
# These go to SUPABASE SECRETS, not Vercel: only edge functions and the local
# copy script ever hold them, and the browser never touches R2 directly (it PUTs
# to a presigned URL issued by `r2-sign-upload`).
#
# All four or none: `r2ConfigFrom` returns null on a partial config and every
# path falls back to Supabase Storage — deploying before R2 exists is a no-op.
# In .env.local these are only needed to run `npm run r2:copy`.
# See infra/README.md for creating the bucket, the token and the CORS rule.
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=your-cloudflare-account-id
# R2_BUCKET=grimoire-assets
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your-r2-access-key-id
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your-r2-secret-access-key

# Stripe — these go to Supabase secrets, NOT Vercel (never prefix with VITE_)
# .env.local is only used to run scripts/stripe-setup.mjs locally.
# Production: supabase secrets set STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_...
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# Set after running: npm run stripe:setup
STRIPE_PRO_MONTHLY_PRICE_ID=price_...
STRIPE_PRO_ANNUAL_PRICE_ID=price_...
